we've all been there we get the great  idea a new project in mind perhaps a new  job opportunity and none of the  questions happen what if I'm not ready  what if I can't do this what if I fail  hello everyone I'm Jesse I'm a  registered nurse and entrepreneur and I  make videos on healthy living and  minimalism in today's video we're going  to talk about how to defeat self-doubt  so that you can be successful whatever  that term means to you so first and  foremost you have to define what success  means to you because it means different  things to different people if you're  gonna work towards a goal but don't know  what that goal is where the final end  result is it's gonna be hard to find  motivation on the way to getting there  and especially when facing difficult  obstacles it is crucial to have a  clearly defined why for what you're  doing what you're doing so the first  thing that I would recommend doing is  take a moment to write down your ideas  for what motivates you is that your  family is that your job is that that you  want to have a greater financial status  what is your reason for why my first tip  is block out the media there's so much  negative information out there about how  horrible the world is and there's so  much good that is happening that you're  not hearing about that negative  information is not gonna help you defeat  self-doubt my second tip for you would  be stay away from toxic relationships  you know those friends the ones that are  always gossiping the ones that you're  not really sure of if they really like  you or not or that you can really trust  they don't exactly motivate you to be a  better person and they're not helping  you to grow either on the other hand tip  number three is find friends that you do  find motivation from people that are  doing things that you want to be doing  or that know the things that you want to  be learning when you find yourself down  or unmotivated these are the people that  are gonna help you get back up on your  feet not the people that are gossiping  or telling you all the ways that it can  go wrong tip number four is constantly  feed yourself with motivation whether  that means prayer for you motivational  YouTube videos podcasts books audio  books the possibilities are endless but  do this often Andrew  keenly tip number five is to journal I  love this one because when I'm angry  when I'm sad when I'm upset for any  reason I can write those things down and  figure out what motivated me to think  that way what made me feel that way by  knowing yourself better you're gonna  know what triggers those negative  thoughts to begin with tip number six is  focus on the positives take time to  write down the things that you are doing  right the things that you're grateful  for by focusing on what is going right  and what you are improving in you will  perhaps see possibilities and  opportunities or perhaps somebody else  will just see risks and along with that  tip number seven is be as specific as  possible with goals don't just wish for  things to happen  make it a plan write it out say I want  to do this by X date when you write it  down you're making yourself accountable  and you're making yourself believe this  is going to happen and this is how I'm  going to do it this next tip I think is  very important in its see failure as an  opportunity for improvement just kind of  adopt that motto because you're going to  make mistakes and if you just dwell on  them instead of learning from them  you're not growing as a person and  you're not gonna get any better and  you're just gonna stay stuck where you  are so when you do make a mistake look  at is a learning opportunity find out  what went wrong and what could I do next  time it's done and it's over with you're  not gonna be able to change the past so  focus on what you can do in the future  this last tip is my favorite by far and  it is take action just do it  there were many occasions in my life  where I questioned myself where I  questioned whether or not my husband and  I could start our own company  successfully where I questioned whether  or not I could be a good nurse where I  questioned whether or not I would be a  good mom the kinds of things that you're  gonna question your self for are gonna  be different but the thing is we all do  these things we're human so just  recognize when they happen and stop them  in their tracks because the truth is  your future is in your hands and you do  have the opportunity to make your life  better I hope you found some of these  tips helpful for you please let me know  which one's your favorite down in the  comments below bye for now  [Music]  hello everyone yes  [Music]
 

